Title: Viva La Vida
Artist: Coldplay
Key: Ab major
Tempo: 136
Time: 4/4

# One four-bar loop — Db Eb Ab Fm, IV V I vi — for essentially the whole record,
# one bar to a chord at 136 bpm.
#
# The key is the point of this entry. Ab major has no open strings on a guitar
# and the record has no guitar on it: the harmony is strings, timpani and a
# church bell. Nothing in a guitar-shaped corpus would catch a system that only
# works in the sharp keys, and a chart of this in G (the capo-friendly reading
# every tab site prints) is four semitones flat — which is a transposition
# finding, not a harmony one.
#
# Note: Ab and Fm share two notes out of three, and the bass drops to Ab under
# the Fm bar. Reading the vi as a second bar of I, or the I as an early vi, is
# the relative-major/minor confusion this corpus exists to keep honest.

